  "description": "The current NetScaler appliance is running with load\u2011balancing (LB) enabled and global server load balancing (GSLB) turned on, while the traditional AAA service is disabled. SSL offloading is active together with SSL VPN, but SSL interception remains off. Adaptive TCP, AppFlow, and Application QoE are all enabled, whereas the Application Firewall and Bot detection modules are disabled. Content filtering (CF) and CloudBridge are turned on, but Content Accelerator and Compression (CMP) are not. The device also has forward\u2011proxy, rewrite, and content switching (CS) features enabled, with HTML injection, HTML rewriting, and HTML compression (SC) disabled where applicable.  \n\nIn the routing and protocol suite, OSPF, RIP, ISIS and BGP are all disabled, as is LSN, while IPv6 protocol translation (IPv6PT) and IPsec (IC) are turned off and on respectively. The system\u2019s security stack includes URL filtering, SSL VPN, and the responder module is disabled; the reputation (REP) engine and priority queuing (PQ) are enabled, whereas the surge\u2011protection (SP) and video\u2011optimization features are off. Push notification, RDP proxy, and push\u2011based NetScaler Push are disabled, while the feature set also confirms that the web\u2011logging (WL) service is active, the firewall (FE0) is not, and the content inspection (CI) and content quality analysis (CQA) are respectively off and on. All remaining flags\u2014such as HDOSP, HTML injection, and other advanced services\u2014are set according to the list above.",
